<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Suleiman the Magnificent</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1494">1494</a>–<a href="/years/1566">1566</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> · Also known as Kanuni</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Suleiman the Magnificent, known in Turkish as Kanuni, the Lawgiver, was Ottoman sultan from 1520 to 1566. He conquered <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/belgrade">Belgrade</a>, won the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-mohacs">Battle of Mohács</a>, besieged <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vienna">Vienna</a> and extended Ottoman power in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mediterranean">Mediterranean</a>. Accounts of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottoman Empire</a> treat his reign as the height of Ottoman power and legal codification.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/suleiman-the-magnificent.jpg" alt="Suleiman the Magnificent" width="320" height="374" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Circle of Titian · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:EmperorSuleiman.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>The Ottoman Sultan <b>Suleiman the Magnificent</b> backed Zápolya, besieged Vienna in 1529 and occupied Buda in 1541, leaving Hungary divided between a Habsburg ‘Royal Hungary’ in the north and west, an Ottoman province in the centre and an autonomous Principality of Transylvania in the east.</blockquote><a href="/empire/habsburg-monarchy">Habsburg Monarchy · Foundation</a></li><li><blockquote>After the Black Army was disbanded in the 1490s the southern fortress line decayed, Belgrade fell in 1521, and on 29 August 1526 <b>Suleiman the Magnificent</b> destroyed the Hungarian army at the Battle of Mohács.</blockquote><a href="/empire/kingdom-of-hungary-1301-1526">Kingdom of Hungary (1301-1526) · Military</a></li><li><blockquote>The reign of <b>Suleiman the Magnificent</b> (r. 1520–1566) produced its most ambitious campaigns: the capture of Belgrade in 1521, the destruction of the Hungarian royal army at the Battle of Mohács in 1526, the first siege of Vienna in 1529, and the naval operations of Hayreddin Barbarossa, whose…</blockquote><a href="/empire/ottoman-empire">Ottoman Empire · Military</a></li><li><blockquote>Later princes had less room: Petru Rareș lost his throne and the Tighina (Bender) region when <b>Suleiman the Magnificent</b> invaded in 1538, and Dimitrie Cantemir’s alliance with Peter the Great ended in the Russian defeat on the Pruth in 1711.</blockquote><a href="/empire/principality-of-moldavia">Principality of Moldavia · Military</a></li><li><blockquote>And at Mohács in 1526 the army of <b>Suleiman the Magnificent</b> destroyed the army of the kingdom of Hungary, whose king died in the retreat.</blockquote><a href="/essays/the-military-revolution">The Military Revolution</a></li><li><blockquote>He governed through the sharia and through kanun, the dynastic law issued in his own name, and <b>Suleiman the Magnificent</b> was remembered as Kanuni, “the Lawgiver”.</blockquote><a href="/societies/ottoman-empire">Social Hierarchy of the Ottoman Empire</a></li></ul></section>
<section class="enc-where enc-born"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Born and died</h2><p class="enc-born-p">Born in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/trabzon">Trabzon</a>, in what is now <a href="/countries/turkey">Turkey</a>. Died in Szigetvár, in what is now <a href="/countries/hungary">Hungary</a>. <span class="enc-born-src">Places as Wikidata records them.</span></p><figure class="st-locator enc-loc"><a href="/atlas?at=41.01,39.72&amp;year=1540" aria-label="Trabzon on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5522 700 900 540" role="img" aria-label="Map: the birthplace of Suleiman the Magnificent"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5972 970h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5972 970h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks the birthplace. <a href="/atlas?at=41.01,39.72&amp;year=1540">What was here in 1540? &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></section>
